Design and Architecture

Block Diagram & Schematic
Below is the block diagram illustrating the system’s hierarchy and the schematic detailing the wiring for the MAN6400 7-segment display and pull-up resistors.


View Block Diagram & Schematic





SystemVerilog Implementation
The design follows a strict hierarchical structure, containing only instantiated modules and simple assign logic at the top level. * seven_segment: A purely combinational decoder utilizing a case statement to map the 4-bit switch input to the corresponding active-low 7-segment display outputs. * counter: A sequential module using a single always_ff block with a hardcoded maximum count parameter to track the \(5,000,000\) cycles necessary for the \(2.4\text{ Hz}\) toggle.


